{{!-- The Season tab: the ritual, assembled.

      It opens on where the wheel stands, then the turn itself — one panel that runs in the order
      Seasons Change prescribes, because the tab's whole job at the table is that procedure. The
      book's spread (Book I, p.85) is still all here; it is filed by when you use it.

      Params: seasons (SeasonsSnapshot). --}}
<div class="steading-seasons">

	{{> "stonetop.steading-season-wheel" turnover=seasons.turnover}}

	{{> "stonetop.steading-season-turn" seasons=seasons}}

	{{!-- After the turn, because it happens after it: the wheel brings the season in, and the harvest
	      or the hunt happens somewhere inside it. --}}
	{{#if seasons.turnover.hasMoments}}
		{{> "stonetop.steading-moments" turnover=seasons.turnover}}
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- The other three seasonal moves, folded away: only one of the four is ever the one the turn
	      rolls, and four cards at equal weight said the opposite. They keep their dice — turning the
	      wheel is what the promoted move's control does, but a table that wants to roll a season's
	      move on its own terms is not something this sheet should decide it cannot. --}}
	{{#if seasons.otherMoves.length}}
		<section class="steading-seasons-others steading-block">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.othersTitle")
			    note=(localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.othersHint")}}
			<ol class="items-list steading-others-list">
				{{#each seasons.otherMoves}}
					{{> "stonetop.move-row" showCheck=false categoryKey=../seasons.moves.key
					    allowAdditional=false alwaysShowResource=false disclosure=true}}
				{{/each}}
			</ol>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

</div>
